125:1-125:11 @[ checks ] ⇒ sect : +U ((a : Path(Circle, Base, Base)) -> -F Path(Path(Circle, Base, Base),⏎  spin(wind(a)), a))⏎⏎Spinning undoes winding at every loop: the round trip at a variable, by⏎induction over the words. The result type reads the word the fold descends⏎on, so each arm answers it at its letter and the recursive call at the⏎rest: `sect[<](q)` relates `spin(wind(q))` to `q`, and carried along⏎`loopOn` it relates `loop ∷ spin(wind(q))`, which `spin(wind(loop ∷ q))`⏎runs to, to `loop ∷ q`. The case respects the cancellations: at `loop ∷⏎back(loop) ∷ q` the arms compose to `cong(loopOn, cong(unloopOn, p))`,⏎whose functions compose to the identity under the words' rules, so the⏎chain is `p` itself, the answer at `q`. @125:1-126:1
